# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PERSONAL TOOLING — Claude Code heartbeat (NOT registry-generated; PRESERVE on
# any regen from cron_registry.yaml — these are intentionally outside the Cron
# Officer's monitored set). 4x/day liveness check. GOVERNED: each line `cd`s into
# ~/tools/claude/ FIRST so it loads AGENTS.md + .claude/settings.json (deny: .py
# writes, DB/sqlite3, systemctl/sudo/service, writes to ~/systems, trading .env
# read, git push) — mirrors AGY. Guardrail files are version-controlled at
# deploy/tools/claude/ (restore on VM rebuild — see disaster recovery doc). Verified 23-Jun.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
30 5 * * * cd /home/ubuntu/tools/claude && /usr/bin/claude -p "Generate a random 8-character string. Print only the string." >> /home/ubuntu/tools/claude/cron.log 2>&1
31 10 * * * cd /home/ubuntu/tools/claude && /usr/bin/claude -p "Generate a random 8-character string. Print only the string." >> /home/ubuntu/tools/claude/cron.log 2>&1
32 15 * * * cd /home/ubuntu/tools/claude && /usr/bin/claude -p "Generate a random 8-character string. Print only the string." >> /home/ubuntu/tools/claude/cron.log 2>&1
33 20 * * * cd /home/ubuntu/tools/claude && /usr/bin/claude -p "Generate a random 8-character string. Print only the string." >> /home/ubuntu/tools/claude/cron.log 2>&1
